{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oxur/vlajmaji/pulls/6","id":5059885504,"node_id":"PR_kwDOVVN6Xs8AAAABLZe5wA","html_url":"https://github.com/oxur/vlajmaji/pull/6","diff_url":"https://github.com/oxur/vlajmaji/pull/6.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/oxur/vlajmaji/pull/6.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oxur/vlajmaji/issues/6","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oxur/vlajmaji/pulls/6/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oxur/vlajmaji/pulls/6/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oxur/vlajmaji/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oxur/vlajmaji/issues/6/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oxur/vlajmaji/statuses/9026c51791b5a356567f78dd9cd3b8c0eb510fa2","number":6,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Add compact and readable dictionary queries with complete-hit detail","user":{"login":"oubiwann","id":894251,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5NDI1MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/894251?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/oubiwann","html_url":"https://github.com/oubiwann","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oubiwann/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oubiwann/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oubiwann/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oubiwann/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oubiwann/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oubiwann/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oubiwann/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oubiwann/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oubiwann/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Dictionary queries can now return compact JSON or readable, source-grouped text, with stable detail references for retrieving complete hits. Full JSON remains the default for both explicit-store and configured lookups.\n\n- Project selected pages before constructing complete hits; preserve occurrence identities, multiplicity, source attribution, totals, cursors, and unavailable/history behavior.\n- Add `dictionary-detail` and `lookup-detail`, optional snapshot checks, and typed readable renderers.\n- Reuse decoded registration metadata while checking current bytes on each call, and index repeated projection lookups.\n- Cover public API and CLI workflows, Linux output-error handling, exclusive test fixtures, and file-backed SQLite mutation input. Document formats and detail commands.\n\nValidation passed: formatting, Clippy, the affected 18-test projection suite, and `make check` (338 Rust tests plus 19 build-helper tests; one corpus-dependent test intentionally ignored). Both [push CI](https://github.com/oxur/vlajmaji/actions/runs/40793790640) and [PR CI](https://github.com/oxur/vlajmaji/actions/runs/40793813316) passed Check, macOS, Linux default, isolated no-default, and all-features gates.\n\nThe first local full check stopped before product code on an `AlreadyExists` temporary-directory setup failure in an unchanged store test. The sole unchanged-source full-check rerun passed; the failure is preserved and the helper remains unchanged.\n\nThe fresh independent technical review accepted the final candidate after checking the assembled public API and 75 CLI cases, including source selection, removal/restoration, stable details, idempotent update and rebuild while preserving old generations. The same reviewer also accepted the canonical closeout records; root verified the final transitions. Slice05 and Arc04 are closed, with the wider project still open and Arc05 unstarted.\n\nReview-method limit: the public checker completed its semantic assertions, but an added timing observer failed on a macOS sysctl permission call and masked the public child exit. That failure and unknown exit remain recorded; no public replay or RSS claim was made. The remaining CLI checks captured real expected exits and passed.\n\nKnown performance limit: the original latency targets were not met. The maintainer accepted current timings; the retained full-data completion passed correctness, output-size, and resource checks, with timing exceptions recorded separately. The metadata byte-comparison optimisation remains a backlog item.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-29T00:24:05Z","updated_at":"2026-10-29T01:13:06Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"97825be7607129de5647396bdba91a7ee633c92e","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"oxur:codex/project01-readable-compact-output","ref":"codex/project01-readable-compact-output","repo":{"id":1431534174,"node_id":"R_kgDOVVN6Xg","name":"vlajmaji","full_name":"oxur/vlajmaji","owner":{"login":"oxur","id":59720599,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjU5NzIwNTk5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/59720599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/oxur","html_url":"https://github.com/oxur","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oxur/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oxur/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oxur/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oxur/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oxur/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oxur/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oxur/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oxur/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oxur/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"private":false,"fork":false,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"description":"(Re)Lojban dictionaries, schemas, library, and CLI tool","homepage":null,"language":"Rust","v